Description: |
  Approximate theory comparison to the neutron A1 column of publication
  Table I and HEPData Table 1. Uses nine published x bins and Q2 windows
  of 2.5, 5 (nominal), and 10 percent around their measured mean Q2.
  Requires Q2 > 1 GeV2, W2 > 4 GeV2, 0 < y < 0.85 and
  0.04 < scattering angle < 0.22 rad; the published outer Q2 range
  ends at 15 GeV2. Detector efficiencies and the experimental x-y
  averaging weights are not reconstructed. Uses free-neutron inputs:
  the data already include the helium-to-neutron extraction. The MC
  estimator uses R1990 fit B and neglects eta*A2, matching the paper's
  central-value treatment; the published systematic error is retained.
  No g1 output or evolution to Q2=2.5 is performed. Windows share events.
